From d1dd61da55a7a712fca1de12abf2c85b923f50b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Run host steps without a terminal

A job on a self-hosted platform (-P label=-self-hosted) runs every step
on a pseudo-terminal, while GitHub's runner gives a step no terminal:
its stdin is empty and its output goes to the log. A step that asks
when it finds a terminal therefore stops at the question under act and
goes on under GitHub. Nix's multi-user installer is one: through
cachix/install-nix-action it waits at "Would you like to see a more
detailed list of what I will do?".

Run the step with the stdin and output exec sets up before the terminal
is allocated.
---
 pkg/container/host_environment.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pkg/container/host_environment.go b/pkg/container/host_environment.go
index 6640222..b8890e2 100644
--- a/pkg/container/host_environment.go
+++ b/pkg/container/host_environment.go
@@ -331,7 +331,7 @@ func (e *HostEnvironment) exec(ctx context.Context, command []string, cmdline st
 			tty.Close()
 		}
 	}()
-	if true /* allocate Terminal */ {
+	if false /* allocate Terminal */ {
 		var err error
 		ppty, tty, err = setupPty(cmd, cmdline)
 		if err != nil {
-- 
